%description:

Tcp.fastopenAcceptWithoutCookie:on -- host2 takes the data of a SYN without a cookie.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "TCP Fast Open, server: accept the data of a SYN without a valid cookie, if the
SYN has data or a Fast Open option, and give no cookie (Linux tcp_fastopen bit 0x200); RFC 7413
requires a valid cookie".

The classes: off (false, the default), on (true), and changed (the parameter is @mutable). The
code: TcpConnection::processSynInListen() takes the data of a SYN without a valid cookie
with true, when the SYN has data or a Fast Open option, and gives no cookie. This test separates "on" from the other value.

Host under test: host2, a Fast Open server (precondition); host1 is a Fast Open client that
sends data on the SYN without a cookie (fastopenClientNoCookieRequired, a precondition): 500
bytes on the SYN of each connection. Observation: level 1, the SYN-ACK acknowledges the SYN and the 500 bytes, and carries no cookie.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenAcceptWithoutCookie
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.fastopenAcceptWithoutCookie
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenAcceptWithoutCookieOn")
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .capture("isn1", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of connection 1, with 500 bytes")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.ackNo == {isn1} + 501")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "-";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN-ACK of host2, without a cookie")
                  .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenAcceptWithoutCookieOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.fastopenAcceptWithoutCookie = true    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientNoCookieRequired = true
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFastopenAcceptWithoutCookieOn: PASS
